1
00:06:48,750 --> 00:06:54,750
Land and Freedom is a war, drama, history film directed by Ken Loach.

2
00:13:37,500 --> 00:13:43,500
David Carr is a British Communist who is unemployed.

3
00:20:26,250 --> 00:20:32,250
In 1936, when the Spanish Civil War begins, he decides to fight for the Republican side, a coalition of liberals, communists and anarchists, so he
joins the POUM militia and witnesses firsthand the betrayal of the Spanish revolution by Stalin's followers and Moscow's orders.

4
00:27:15,000 --> 00:27:21,000
David Carr, played by Ian Hart.

5
00:34:03,750 --> 00:34:09,750
Blanca, played by Rosana Pastor.

6
00:40:52,500 --> 00:40:58,500
Bernard, played by Frédéric Pierrot.

7
00:47:41,250 --> 00:47:47,250
Maite, played by Icíar Bollaín.

8
00:54:30,000 --> 00:54:36,000
Lawrence, played by Tom Gilroy.

9
01:01:18,750 --> 01:01:24,750
Kitty, played by Angela Clarke.

10
01:08:07,500 --> 01:08:13,500
Land and Freedom (or Tierra y Libertad) is a 1995 film
directed by Ken Loach and written by Jim Allen.

11
01:14:56,250 --> 01:15:02,250
The film narrates the story of David Carr, an unemployed worker and member of the Communist Party of Great Britain,
who decides to fight in the Spanish Civil War for the republicans against a nationalist coup d'état.

12
01:21:45,000 --> 01:21:51,000
The film won the FIPRESCI International Critics Prize and the Prize of
the Ecumenical Jury at the 1995 Cannes Film Festival.

13
01:28:33,750 --> 01:28:39,750
The film was also nominated for the Palme d'Or at Cannes.

14
01:35:22,500 --> 01:35:28,500
The film explores themes of worker, spain, solidarity, revolution, fascism.

15
01:42:11,250 --> 01:42:17,250
The tone is emotional.
